{
  "_why": "Role track for CNC GRINDING, the third pack authored under docs/profiling/role-pack-authoring-guide.md and the first of Batch 1's new packs. fam_machining stays the generic machining interview bound at ISCO unit 7223; this pack binds the NCO grinding occupations directly (job_domain specificity 50 beats unit 40), so a grinder gets grinding depth and every other machining worker is untouched.",
  "_scope": "CNC AND CONVENTIONAL, on the same ruling that shaped qp_cnc_turning. The taxonomy lists 'CNC vs conventional' as this role's own attribute rather than as two roles, and a surface-grinder hand who has never seen a controller must be able to answer every question here honestly: grinding_type asks which he runs, controller_brand carries a 'Pata nahi' escape, and the machine list leads with the conventional surface grinder. The gate says 'Grinding', not 'CNC grinding', for the same reason the turner's says 'Turning'.",
  "_depth": "THE TIER GATE IS grinding_experience, asked FIRST. It cannot be experience_years from qp_universal: phase order runs occupation_specific BEFORE universal_tail, so the universal answer does not exist yet when these items are selected. Its options carry value_number ONLY. pack-registry.service.ts resolves valueText ?? valueNumber ?? valueBool, so adding a value_text would make the answer a STRING; every gte below would then compare a string to a number, compare() returns null, and the predicate is false forever. A permanently-false ask_if is a question that is never asked, silently -- the #776 defect that sat in qp_welding for the life of the pack.",
  "_budget": "MAX_ENGINE_ASKS is 28 and qp_universal spends 8. Tier 0 is 8 items (16 total), tier 1 adds 3 (19), tier 2 adds 4 (23). The three fresher items are gated on grinding_experience <= 0 and a senior never sees them; a fresher skips tiers 1 and 2 entirely, so his worst case is 16 + 3 = 19. The tiers are mutually exclusive by construction, which is why the fresher branch costs the senior nothing.",
  "_sheet": "SECTION B IS READ OFF THE RATIFIED REFERENCE SHEET (Sanjay Kamble, CNC Grinding Operator -- Setter), not invented. Its ten rows are Machines, Controllers, Materials, Setting, Measuring instruments, Wheels dressed, Drawings, Tolerance held, Surface finish held and Sector worked, and every one has a question here that fills it. Tolerance and surface finish are BANDED single-selects rather than free numbers: the sheet prints '+/-0.005 mm' and 'Ra 0.4 um', which are bands, and a banded chip keeps a low-literacy worker tapping instead of typing while avoiding the answer_type 'number' path that has no Flutter widget.",
  "pack_id": "qp_cnc_grinding",
  "version": 1,
  "family_id": "fam_cnc_grinding",
  "locale": "hi-IN",
  "status": "active",
  "review_note": "Drafted for owner review (Prakash). Shop-floor vocabulary NOT yet corrected by a practising grinder -- see docs/registers/trade-content-ratification.md.",
  "_fresher": "Guideline section 11 #1: a fresher's Zone 4 is training, trade test, machines used in the ITI workshop and project work, and the History heading never renders empty. These three items are the ask half; resume-fresher-rows.ts, fed by this role's descriptor, is the render half.",
  "items": [
